  "family": "pop",
  "lineage": "Late-1990s and 2000s R&B subgenre developed in Philadelphia (Roots, Jill Scott, Musiq Soulchild) and broader American urban scenes, characterized by live-instrument analog production (vs the parallel commercial R&B's drum-machine production), jazz-and-soul-influenced harmonic vocabulary, and reverent reference to 1970s classic soul aesthetic. D'Angelo's Voodoo (2000), Erykah Badu's Baduizm (1997), and Maxwell's Embrya (1998) consolidated the canonical sound. The Soulquarians collective (Questlove, J Dilla, D'Angelo, Erykah Badu, Common, Mos Def, Bilal, Q-Tip) anchored the artistic-organizational hub.",
